 "transcript": "Do not vibe code your app unless you've created these six documents. First is your PRD, your product requirements document. It lays out every feature and exactly what you're building, along with a brief overview of the whole app idea. Number two is your TRD, your technical requirements document. Put your technical decisions here, the stack, tools, and APIs you plan to use. It gives your agent a blueprint to make technical decisions without guessing. Third is app flow. Map the phases of your app, how navigation and the user journey work, and what happens when someone clicks a button, including what page comes next. Fourth is the UI slash UX design brief. The apps look and feel, color palette, typography, components, style, and roughly how each screen should look. So the AI has direction instead of building something random. Fifth is backend schema. Show how user data is stored and organized, including the authentication flow and every table, its columns and relationships. Sixth is implementation plan. Spell out the exact step -by -step build sequence so the AI agent knows in which order to build your app. You can use Claude or ChatGPT to build these documents. Together, they help your agent understand your app better. Comment docs and I'll send you the documents I've personally been using.",
